{
  "_comment": [
    "Registry backends for TLDs the IANA RDAP bootstrap does not cover (or covers badly).",
    "status: rdap | whois | restricted | unavailable.",
    "rdap: base URL (base + 'domain/<fqdn>'); null with status rdap means 'use the IANA bootstrap'.",
    "whois: port-43 server; with status rdap it is only a fallback if RDAP resolution yields nothing.",
    "Only entries verified live (a registered name vs a random one) may be rdap/whois: a wrong",
    "not_found pattern produces false 'available' results.",
    "reason: user-facing explanation, required for restricted/unavailable."
  ],
  "rdap_denylist": {
    "tlds": [
      "gg",
      "la"
    ],
    "reason": "rdap.gg answers every name with an HTML 200 page; rdap.centralnic.com/la/ answers 404 for everything (even google.la). Both go to WHOIS instead."
  },
